{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNXxNeix2oYQiCqFQQpG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R32itGVQRjn8g5c3itqqWF","name":"mcp__week1-wire__check_claims","input":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Kenny Nguyen, the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, which supersedes SR 11-7 (2011) and SR 21-8 (2021) and calls for a risk-based approach tailored to each organization's model risk profile. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter says it is expected to be most relevant to Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 (Model Risk Management) covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 expects an enterprise model inventory that includes vendor and third-party models, and monitoring for autonomous decision-making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 (Technology and Cyber Risk Management) sets expectations for federally regulated financial institutions. [src-osfi-b13]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n\n- Confirm: SR 26-2 applicability requires confirmation. The letter addresses Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations and is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion in total assets; confirm whether Northbridge Financial Group has one. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n\n- Canadian domestic systemically important bank, about USD 900 billion in total assets, and an existing Forge customer. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Agents are in production and a risk committee is on record; whether it has a US Federal Reserve-regulated entity is unknown. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n\n- \"Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools.\" [P-GATEWAY]\n- \"Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide.\" [P-EVIDENCE]\n- \"Reign Assurance is in co-design development.\" [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n- \"iTmethods does not validate its own work, independently review it or subject it to effective challenge, and does not certify, attest, issue an audit opinion or provide independent assurance, so where any of those functions is required, we would work with a firm that holds that mandate.\" [P-BANKING]\n\n## Suggested next step\n\nOffer the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how agents already in production would appear in an E-23 model inventory before May 1, 2027.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n\n- Avery Lindqvist (fictional), Chief Audit Executive [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001]\n- Morgan Achebe (fictional), Chief Risk Officer [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002]\n- Priya Raman (fictional), Head of Model Risk Management [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003]\n- Daniel Okafor (fictional), VP, Platform Engineering [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004]\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n\n- Does Northbridge have a US banking entity supervised by the Federal Reserve? Until that is known, SR 26-2 applicability requires confirmation.\n- Does Northbridge have EU entities that DORA covers?\n- Are the production agents already in the model inventory, and who owns them?\n- The Chief Information Security Officer was not routed: the title matches the do-not-route list. Decide whether that relationship is handled separately.\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\n\n**Risk (audit, model risk, evidence):** E-23 brings AI and machine learning models, including vendor models, into the enterprise inventory from May 1, 2027, and Northbridge already runs agents in production. The question for the Chief Audit Executive and Head of Model Risk Management is what evidence exists today for each agent: owner, risk rating, and monitoring for autonomous behaviour. Any SR 26-2 angle waits on confirming a US Federal Reserve-regulated entity.\n\n**Engineering (runtime, governed path for agent calls):** Northbridge already runs Forge, so the platform team knows the estate. The question for the VP, Platform Engineering is whether production agents reach models and tools through one governed path that records what was called, by which agent, under which approval, so the risk lane has the record it needs.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-osfi-e23] OSFI Guideline E-23 - Model Risk Management (2027) - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/guideline-e-23-model-risk-management-2027\n- [src-osfi-b13] OSFI Guideline B-13 - Technology and Cyber Risk Management - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/technology-cyber-risk-management\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-BANKING] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/sectors/banking\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1001] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004] ZoomInfo contact record"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3109,"cache_read_input_tokens":41297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3109},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fdad30-284c-4421-8ab8-20f5f20c459b","uuid":"a232fc8a-761d-432a-b045-821c727a6a17","timestamp":"2026-09-24T15:54:10.561Z","request_id":"req_011CfNXxN8iLMU6rGxLWpnsY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01R32itGVQRjn8g5c3itqqWF":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Kenny Nguyen, the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, which supersedes SR 11-7 (2011) and SR 21-8 (2021) and calls for a risk-based approach tailored to each organization's model risk profile. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter says it is expected to be most relevant to Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 (Model Risk Management) covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 expects an enterprise model inventory that includes vendor and third-party models, and monitoring for autonomous decision-making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 (Technology and Cyber Risk Management) sets expectations for federally regulated