{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNXzmwkiX4WK3zCuaTv4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HjAJJ3TQedGspxeHoUJ8HW","name":"mcp__week1-wire__check_claims","input":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Kenny Nguyen, the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, replacing SR 11-7 (2011) and SR 21-8 (2021) with a risk-based approach tailored to each organization's model risk profile. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 (Model Risk Management) covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 expects an enterprise model inventory that includes vendor and third-party models, with monitoring for autonomous decision-making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 (Technology and Cyber Risk Management) sets expectations for federally regulated financial institutions. [src-osfi-b13]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n\n- Confirm: SR 26-2 applicability requires confirmation. The letter addresses Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations and is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion in total assets; confirm whether Northbridge Financial Group has one. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n\n- Canadian domestic systemically important bank with about USD 900 billion in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Existing Forge customer. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Agents are in production and a risk committee is on record; a US Federal Reserve-regulated entity is not on record. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- Reign Assurance is in co-design development. [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n- iTmethods does not validate its own work, independently review it or subject it to effective challenge, and does not certify, attest, issue an audit opinion or provide independent assurance, so where any of those functions is required, we would work with a firm that holds that mandate. [P-BANKING]\n\n## Suggested next step\n\n- Offer the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how the agents already in production would sit in an E-23 model inventory ahead of May 1, 2027.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n- Risk lane: Avery Lindqvist (fictional), Chief Audit Executive [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001]; Morgan Achebe (fictional), Chief Risk Officer [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002]; Priya Raman (fictional), Head of Model Risk Management [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003]\n- Engineering lane: Daniel Okafor (fictional), VP, Platform Engineering [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004]\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n\n- Does Northbridge have a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve? Until that is known, SR 26-2 applicability requires confirmation.\n- Does Northbridge have EU entities of the types DORA covers?\n- Are the production agents in the bank's model inventory today, and who owns each one?\n- One contact was not routed because the title matches the do-not-route list for information security.\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\n\n**Risk (audit, model risk, evidence):** From May 1, 2027, E-23 puts AI and machine learning models, vendor models included, into the enterprise inventory, and Northbridge already has agents in production. The useful question for the Chief Audit Executive and the Head of Model Risk Management is what record exists today for each agent: owner, risk rating, and monitoring for autonomous behaviour and drift. Any SR 26-2 angle waits until a US Federal Reserve-regulated entity is confirmed.\n\n**Engineering (runtime, governed path for agent calls):** The platform team already runs the estate these agents sit on. The question for the VP, Platform Engineering is whether production agents reach models and tools through one governed path that records which agent called what, under which approval, so the risk lane has a record to work from.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-osfi-e23] OSFI Guideline E-23 - Model Risk Management (2027) - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/guideline-e-23-model-risk-management-2027\n- [src-osfi-b13] OSFI Guideline B-13 - Technology and Cyber Risk Management - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/technology-cyber-risk-management\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-BANKING] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/sectors/banking\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1001] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004] ZoomInfo contact record"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":58160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":353},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fdad30-284c-4421-8ab8-20f5f20c459b","uuid":"387f1490-2687-406f-bdaa-509b94ab80da","timestamp":"2026-09-24T15:54:44.235Z","request_id":"req_011CfNXzmVDNDwhk8ER2xGuv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HjAJJ3TQedGspxeHoUJ8HW":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Kenny Nguyen, the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, replacing SR 11-7 (2011) and SR 21-8 (2021) with a risk-based approach tailored to each organization's model risk profile. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 (Model Risk Management) covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 expects an enterprise model inventory that includes vendor and third-party models, with monitoring for autonomous decision-making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 (Technology and Cyber Risk Management) sets expectations for federally regulated financial institutions. [src-osfi-b13]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n\n- Confirm: SR 26-2 applicability requires confirmation. The letter addresses Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations and is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion in total assets; confirm whether Northbridge Financial Group has one. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n\n- Canadian domestic systemically important bank with about USD 900 billion in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Existing Forge customer. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Agents are in production and a risk committee is on record; a US Federal Reserve-regulated entity is not on record. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- Reign Assurance is in co-design development. [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n- iTmethods does not validate its own work, independently review it or subject it to effective challenge, and does not certify, attest, issue an audit opinion or provide independent assurance, so where any of those functions is required, we would work with a firm that holds that mandate. [P-BANKING]\n\n## Suggested next step\n\n- Offer the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how the agents already in production would sit in an E-23 model inventory ahead of May 1, 2027.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n- Risk lane: Avery Lindqvist (fictional), Chief Audit Executive [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001]; Morgan Achebe (fictional), Chief Risk Officer [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002]; Priya Raman (fictional), Head of Model Risk Management [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003]\n- Engineering lane: Daniel Okafor (fictional), VP, Platform Engineering [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004]\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n\n- Does Northbridge have a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve? Until that is known, SR 26-2 applicability requires confirmation.\n- Does Northbridge have EU entities of the types DORA covers?\n- Are the production agents in the bank's model inventory today, and who owns each one?\n- One contact was not routed because the title matches the do-not-route list for information security.\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\n\n**Risk (audit, model risk, evidence):** From May 1, 2027, E-23 puts AI and machine learning models, vendor models included, into the enterprise inventory, and Northbridge already has agents in production. The useful question for the Chief Audit Executive and the Head of Model Risk Management is what record exists today for each agent: owner, risk rating, and monitoring for autonomous behaviour and drift. Any SR 26-2 angle waits until a US Federal Reserve-regulated entity is confirmed.\n\n**Engineering (runtime, governed path for agent calls):** The platform team already runs the estate these agents sit on. The question for the VP, Platform Engineering is whether production agents reach models and tools through one governed path that records which agent called what, under which approval, so the risk lane has a record to work from.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-osfi-e23] OSFI Guideline E-23 - Model Risk Management (2027) - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/guideline-e-23-model-risk-management-2027\n- [src-osfi-b13] OSFI Guideline B-13 - Technology and Cyber Risk Management - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/technology-cyber-risk-management\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-BANKING] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/sectors/banking\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1001] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004] ZoomInfo contact record"}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HjAJJ3TQedGspxeHoUJ8HW","display_name":"Check Claims","server_display_name":"week1-wire"}]}
