{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNY3Z3gdWP2pcQk7xTMH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"hs-1001 passes. Now drafting hs-1002 (Lakeshore, US bank holding company, USD 85 billion in assets, Federal Reserve-regulated entity on record, agents planned, not a Forge customer)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3488,"cache_read_input_tokens":62773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3488},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fdad30-284c-4421-8ab8-20f5f20c459b","uuid":"53cc9c76-c203-4d9f-9865-249cb2ec77a2","timestamp":"2026-09-24T15:55:05.657Z","request_id":"req_011CfNY3YWSmS7uK8fbmorSY"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNY3Z3gdWP2pcQk7xTMH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PKVvX8DRm61brLKnZ5q2md","name":"mcp__week1-wire__check_claims","input":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1002","brief_markdown":"# Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Kenny Nguyen, the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, replacing SR 11-7 and SR 21-8 with a risk-based approach to model risk. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter calls for model risk practices tailored to each organization's model risk profile and the size and complexity of its operations. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n\n- SR 26-2 says it is expected to be most relevant to Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets. [src-sr26-2]\n- Lakeshore's record shows about USD 85 billion in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1002]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp's banking organizations are regulated by the Federal Reserve, and their total assets; the letter is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp has EU entities of the types DORA covers; that depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n\n- US bank holding company with about 12,000 employees. [hubspot:company/hs-1002]\n- The enrichment record marks a Federal Reserve-regulated entity, agents as planned rather than in production, and a risk committee. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- iTmethods does not validate its own work, independently review it or subject it to effective challenge, and does not certify, attest, issue an audit opinion or provide independent assurance, so where any of those functions is required, we would work with a firm that holds that mandate. [P-BANKING]\n\n## Suggested next step\n\n- Offer the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how planned agents would enter model risk management under SR 26-2 before they reach production.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n- Risk lane: Jordan Whitfield (fictional), Chief Risk Officer [zoominfo:contact/zi-2006]\n- Engineering lane: Casey Nakamura (fictional), Head of AI Engineering [zoominfo:contact/zi-2007]\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n\n- The Federal Reserve-regulated entity comes from the enrichment row; can the account owner confirm it and name the entity?\n- Does Lakeshore have EU entities of the types DORA covers?\n- Which agent use cases are planned, and would the bank treat them as models in its inventory?\n- No chief audit executive is on record in the routed contacts; is there one in the existing relationship?\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\n\n**Risk (model risk, audit, evidence):** SR 26-2 replaces SR 11-7, the letter Lakeshore's model risk program was likely built around, and asks for an approach sized to the bank's own model risk profile. With agents still planned, the Chief Risk Officer can decide how agents are classified, inventoried and monitored before the first one ships, rather than retrofitting a record afterwards.\n\n**Engineering (runtime, governed path for agent calls):** The Head of AI Engineering is designing the agent runtime now. The question is whether every agent reaches models and tools through one governed path that records which agent called what, under which approval, so the risk lane has a record from day one.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-BANKING] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/sectors/banking\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1002] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2006] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2007] ZoomInfo contact record"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3488,"cache_read_input_tokens":62773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3488},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fdad30-284c-4421-8ab8-20f5f20c459b","uuid":"4fd10a1f-6ca7-4288-b9ed-d4da7453ac5a","timestamp":"2026-09-24T15:55:17.482Z","request_id":"req_011CfNY3YWSmS7uK8fbmorSY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PKVvX8DRm61brLKnZ5q2md":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1002","brief_markdown":"# Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Kenny Nguyen, the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, replacing SR 11-7 and SR 21-8 with a risk-based approach to model risk. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter calls for model risk practices tailored to each organization's model risk profile and the size and complexity of its operations. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n\n- SR 26-2 says it is expected to be most relevant to Federal Reserve-regulated banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets. [src-sr26-2]\n- Lakeshore's record shows about USD 85 billion in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1002]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp's banking organizations are regulated by the Federal Reserve, and their total assets; the letter is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp has EU entities of the types DORA covers; that depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n\n- US bank holding company with about 12,000 employees. [hubspot:company/hs-1002]\n- The enrichment record marks a Federal Reserve-regulated entity, agents as planned rather than in production, and a risk committee. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- iTmethods does not validate its own work, independently review it or subject it to effective challenge, and does not certify, attest, issue an audit opinion or provide independent assurance, so where any of those functions is required, we would work with a firm that holds that mandate. [P-BANKING]\n\n## Suggested next step\n\n- Offer the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how planned agents would enter model risk management under SR 26-2 before they reach production.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n- Risk lane: Jordan Whitfield (fictional), Chief Risk Officer [zoominfo:contact/zi-2006]\n- Engineering lane: Casey Nakamura (fictional), Head of AI Engineering [zoominfo:contact/zi-2007]\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n\n- The Federal Reserve-regulated entity comes from the enrichment row; can the account owner confirm it and name the entity?\n- Does Lakeshore have EU entities of the types DORA covers?\n- Which agent use cases are planned, and would the bank treat them as models in its inventory?\n- No chief audit executive is on record in the routed contacts; is there one in the existing relationship?\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\n\n**Risk (model risk, audit, evidence):** SR 26-2 replaces SR 11-7, the letter Lakeshore's model risk program was likely built around, and asks for an approach sized to the bank's own model risk profile. With agents still planned, the Chief Risk Officer can decide how agents are classified, inventoried and monitored before the first one ships, rather than retrofitting a record afterwards.\n\n**Engineering (runtime, governed path for agent calls):** The Head of AI Engineering is designing the agent runtime now. The question is whether every agent reaches models and tools through one governed path that records which agent called what, under which approval, so the risk lane has a record from day one.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-BANKING] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/sectors/banking\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1002] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2006] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2007] ZoomInfo contact record"}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PKVvX8DRm61brLKnZ5q2md","display_name":"Check Claims","server_display_name":"week1-wire"}]}
