 skill rule says never state that, so it stays a \"Confirm\" line. The Federal Reserve-regulated flag comes only from the enrichment record, and I listed it as an open question for you.\n- **Only the SR 26-2 cover page was read.** The detailed guidance is in an attached PDF that couldn't be read as text. The briefs use only what the cover letter says: the supersessions, the $30B threshold and the risk-based approach. They say nothing about how SR 26-2 treats AI.\n- **Northbridge's information-security chief was left off.** That contact matches the do-not-route list. The brief doesn't name them and mentions it only as an open question.\n- **Lakeshore has no chief audit executive in the routed contacts,** so its risk lane is the Chief Risk Officer only.\n- **Forge isn't mentioned for Lakeshore.** The checker allows product names only in approved wording, so the brief doesn't say that Lakeshore isn't a Forge customer.\n\nI didn't run `python3 -m evals.score_run` on these briefs. I also didn't add entries to `PROCESS-LOG.md` or commit anything. Say if you want either done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5478,"cache_read_input_tokens":69590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5478},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5fdad30-284c-4421-8ab8-20f5f20c459b","uuid":"72810c43-7811-48d9-a04a-9b8e44d10e93","timestamp":"2026-09-24T15:55:56.819Z","request_id":"req_011CfNY6pPFr5ZUDTbEbRpNb"}
